      "evidence_id": "S2P2",
      "text": "This cheat sheet provides guidance on implementing transport layer protection for applications using Transport Layer Security (TLS). It primarily focuses on how to use TLS to protect clients connecting to a web application over HTTPS, though much of this guidance is also applicable to other uses of TLS. When correctly implemented, TLS can provide several security benefits:"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "S2P3",
      "text": "- **Confidentiality**: Provides protection against attackers reading the contents of the traffic.\n- **Integrity**: Provides protection against traffic tampering, such as an attacker modifying or replaying intercepted requests against the server.\n- **Authentication**: Enables the client to confirm they are connected to the legitimate server. Note that the identity of the client is not verified unless client certificates are employed."
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "S3P1",
